  "reviewed_by": "Claude: Butler check summaries in the main Butler chat",
  "reason": "Each finished Butler check (Nebula-wide, project periodic, event-triggered) now posts one summary to the main Butler chat. butler_recovery saves Butler's final reply on the case (check_summary) and, when _update_case finishes a case, calls the new butler_check_summary module; process_project also publishes recently finished undecided cases and delivers queued summaries. The case's summary_post marker and a case-derived message id make it exactly-once; 'No change' (resolved, no structured change, reply first line 'No change') and checks that never ran post nothing. Summaries are queued on the shared ButlerGlobalState row (new fields: target project/session, last fallback, bounded outbox) because a project worker may write only its own rows; the target project's worker inserts an assistant message (metadata.kind=butler_check_summary, no turn, not operator input). Target: configured chat, else the global-check anchor project's Butler chat, else the newest ButlerFocusRuntime chat, else the check's own project Butler chat; unavailable targets fall back and are recorded. GET/PUT /butler/check-interval gains summary_target (no new UI API call signature); the Settings check-interval card gains a summary-chat selector; settings catalog, settings-assistant doc and product knowledge updated; runtime-compatibility entity_fields_sha256 updated for the added fields. Python selects the new suite, the recovery/capabilities/concurrent/capacity/home-host recovery suites, the instructions route, settings gateway, host routes, domain, runtime bundle, CRUD classification, tolerant readers and product-knowledge digest plus the new and related help rows; Frontend selects the check-interval card, settings list/page and Butler host catalog tests.",
  "exclusions": "Node ids exclude failures on unmodified main: test_butler_recovery.py::test_act_switches_worker_to_provider_and_queues_only_the_parent, test_butler_capabilities.py::test_scheduled_butler_can_edit_all_assistant_settings, test_tolerant_entity_readers.py::test_a_new_entity_field_needs_a_reviewed_addition_flag. test_butler_workflow_registry.py (3 unreviewed signatures in butlerBoard.ts/useProjectViewLease.ts), test_settings_assistant_tools.py (destination count, host-command tools) and test_product_knowledge.py::test_product_search_finds_headless_core_and_paired_butler_cli fail on unmodified main and are not selected. UI API call signatures are unchanged (the PUT goes through one helper with the same path and method), so the Butler workflow inventory is unchanged. No native, Playwright or live Core check; no full-suite approval.",
